# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Environment variables — names and meaning only. Copy to .env.local for dev;
# set real values in Railway → Variables. Never commit a real value.
#
# One deployment serves TWO products with separate mail identities:
#   • Festive Frames (holiday kit, /build)  → EMAIL_FROM, ADMIN_ORDER_EMAIL, PRODUCTION_EMAILS
#   • MySchoolFrame  (/school, /s/<slug>)  → MSF_EMAIL_FROM, MSF_ORDER_EMAIL
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Stripe (server only)
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# Canonical origin. The code's SITE_URL constant lives in src/config/season.ts.
SITE_URL=

# Postgres (school ledger, brand cache, school requests). Memory store when unset.
DATABASE_URL=

# ── Mail (Resend). Nothing sends until RESEND_API_KEY is set. ──
RESEND_API_KEY=

# Festive Frames holiday kit — unchanged.
# EMAIL_FROM must be on a domain verified in Resend.
EMAIL_FROM=
ADMIN_ORDER_EMAIL=
# Comma-separated founder inboxes for holiday production emails.
PRODUCTION_EMAILS=

# MySchoolFrame — every school email: paid school orders, "send it to us" designs,
# "we don't have my school" requests, school failure alerts, and the bcc on a
# parent's confirmation. Comma-separated. Default when unset: bill@myschoolframe.com
# (SCHOOL_CONTACT_EMAIL in src/content/school-contact.ts).
MSF_ORDER_EMAIL=
# MySchoolFrame sender, e.g. MySchoolFrame <orders@myschoolframe.com>.
# LEAVE UNSET until myschoolframe.com is verified in Resend (Domains → add, then the
# DKIM/SPF DNS records). Unset, school mail goes out from EMAIL_FROM's verified
# mailbox under the name "MySchoolFrame", so orders keep flowing. Setting it before
# the domain verifies makes every school email fail to send.
MSF_EMAIL_FROM=
